The OpenStreetMap data in this folder (raw/osm.pbf, and the files in build/
that come from it) is a Derivative Database of OpenStreetMap.

© OpenStreetMap contributors.

It is available under the Open Database License 1.0 (ODbL):
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

The corrections in overrides.json are a part of this Derivative Database, and
are also under the ODbL 1.0.

The height data (raw/dem.tif, and the height files in build/height/) comes from
the Copernicus DEM GLO-30:

produced using Copernicus WorldDEM-30 © DLR e.V. 2010-2014 and © Airbus Defence
and Space GmbH 2014-2018 provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and
ESA; all rights reserved.

The organisations in charge of the Copernicus programme by law or by delegation
do not incur any liability for any use of the Copernicus WorldDEM-30.

Plan 0009 (R5): the sources of the buildings and of the lidar points.

- The buildings theme of Overture Maps (raw/buildings/overture.json, and
  build/buildings_2019.json): © OpenStreetMap contributors, Overture Maps
  Foundation, Microsoft, Google, and the other sources of the theme; the
  Open Database License 1.0 (ODbL).
- Google Open Buildings 2.5D Temporal (raw/buildings/temporal_*.tif, and the
  heights and the first years of build/buildings_2019.json): Google, under
  the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 license (CC BY 4.0). Open Buildings
  has two licenses (CC BY 4.0 and ODbL); the game uses CC BY 4.0 for the
  2.5D rasters, and the outlines of Google Open Buildings v3 come in the
  theme of Overture Maps under the ODbL.
- OpenStreetMap on 2019-01-22 from the ohsome API of HeiGIT
  (raw/buildings/osm2019.json): © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL.
- The lidar points of ICESat-2 (ATL03, ATL08, ATL24) and GEDI (L2A) from the
  public service of SlideRule (raw/lidar/): the data of NASA, free to use
  with no restriction; the credit is NASA, the National Snow and Ice Data
  Center, and the Land Processes DAAC, and SlideRule (University of
  Washington and NASA).
